  ],
  "rationale": "<p>The correct answer is <math alttext=\"39,000\"><mn>39,000</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that the giant armadillo has a mass of <math alttext=\"39\"><mn>39</mn>\n</math> kilograms. Since <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> kilogram is equal to <math alttext=\"1,000\"><mn>1,000</mn>\n</math> grams, <math alttext=\"39\"><mn>39</mn>\n</math> kilograms&nbsp;is equal to <math alttext=\"39 kilograms left parenthesis StartFraction 1,000 grams Over 1 kilogram EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mn>39</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>kilograms</mtext><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>1,000</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>grams</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>kilogram</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"39,000\"><mn>39,000</mn>\n</math> grams. Therefore, the giant armadillo&rsquo;s mass, in grams, is <math alttext=\"39,000\"><mn>39,000</mn>\n</math>.</p>",
